{"kind":"assert","text":"Rulings on 58b730b1 and 5fa54dd6 for the cutover head (05d618e2).\n\nP1. Ruling e7787de0, item 5, covers it. The three browser custody\nrecords of claim.ts, connection-custody.ts and oauth-custody.ts\nare stores that the code names, so they are case A. Each takes a\nnew storage name, and its config is `v: 2`. The new Page reads no\nold name. If one of the three was not in rows 14, 15 and 18, add\nit to the list in the note.\n\nT1. A made-up genesis digest is allowed where the code under test\nnever admits the sequence and never compares it with an admitted\none: a codec round trip, a wire shape, a route by address. Where\nthe code under test admits a genesis or reads a sequence, the test\nuses real genesis bytes.\n\nT2, both cases. A hand-written genesis passes ruling 5 when the\nreal `admitSequenceGenesis` admits its bytes. That is the\ncondition that matters. So the checkers stage fixture stays, and\ncheckers gains no dependency. The support-origin lanes, the\nsource-name child and the invitations inbox stay too.\n`scriptedSequence` remains the helper for a genesis with no\nsource. Add a variant with a source and a creator only if three\nor more sites in one package write the same shape.\n\nT3.\n(a) Keep the kind, and do not drop the column. The replay reads\n    the genesis, so it holds the kind. The coverage row carries it\n    as its own member beside the reference, and the text of `dap\n    verify` still says \"directory\". A coverage row that does not\n    include entry 0 carries no kind.\n(b) As you state.\n(c) Record it again with the Scope recorder. Do the same for\n    cli application-release-listing.json. The note names the\n    command for each.\n(d) The plain reference, with no kind.\n\nThe three cli tests that now compare the full reference are\nright.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}